    "introduction": "Beppe Tufarulo is a multi-award-winning Italian writer and director based in Milan. After starting out at MTV, he carved out a path as a filmmaker, making documentaries and forays into narrative film. His hallmark is a heightened visual sensibility and a concern with stories that are more intimate and deeply human. Tufarulo’s documentaries exploring the worlds of music, sports, and fashion include Ferro, All or Nothing: Juventus, Armani Privé – A View Beyond, Una favola siciliana, and Puglia: Appunti di viaggio. His shorts Baradar and We’ll Let You Know have received numerous international awards. The Craft marks his feature directorial debut.",
